{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"skill acquisition skill acquisition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md","fileName":"Skill Acquisition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Skill Acquisition","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human Cognition]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Long-Term Memory","Virtual Environment","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"skill acquisition skill acquisition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md","fileName":"Skill Acquisition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Skill Acquisition","heading":"Skill Acquisition","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Skill acquisition is the process through which repeated performance makes actions faster, more accurate, and less dependent on conscious attention.\n\nThe cognitive stage relies on explicit instructions and deliberate thought. The associative stage tunes behavior and reduces errors. In the autonomous stage, actions can be executed rapidly and accurately with little conscious control. Acquired skills are stored as procedural knowledge in [[Long-Term Memory]].\n\nFor training in a [[Virtual Environment]], an important question is whether a skill learned through the interface transfers to performance in the physical world.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Long-Term Memory","Virtual Environment","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Skill Acquisition.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Fu